      "problem": "$(32+(-4)\\times 7)^{3}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe begin by performing the operations inside the parentheses. So, first we multiply $(-4)$ by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(32+(-4)\\times 7)^{3} & =(32+(-28))^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we add the numbers inside the parentheses: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(32+(-28))^{3} & ={4}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the exponent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{3}=64\\end{aligned}\n$$",
